%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Model a block on a moving conveyor belt anchored to a wall by a spring. Compare positions and velocities for the different values of the parameters of the system (mass of the block, belt speed, friction coefficient, spring constant):

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Model a block on a moving conveyor belt anchored to a wall by a spring. Compare positions and velocities for the different values of the parameters of the system (mass of the block, belt speed, friction coefficient, spring constant):

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
ClearAll[m];

beltv[t_] = vb;
spring[x_] = k (l - x);
friction[v_] := -a (v - beltv[t]);

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Newton's equation for the block:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Newton's equation for the block:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
sys := {
  m x''[t] == spring[x[t]] + friction[x'[t]], 
  x[0] == l, 
  x'[0] == 0
};

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Solve for position and velocity:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Solve for position and velocity:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
sol = DSolve[sys, x, t];

{pos[m_, k_, a_, vb_, t_], vel[m_, k_, a_, vb_, t_]} = {x[t], x'[t]} /. sol[[1]] // FullSimplify;

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
The block stabilizes just above the spring's natural length of l:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
The block stabilizes just above the spring's natural length of l:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
l = 1;
Manipulate[{Plot[{pos[m, k, a, vb, t]}, {t, 0, 2}, PlotRange -> All, 
   PlotLabel -> "Position"], 
  Plot[{vel[m, k, a, vb, t], vb}, {t, 0, 2}, PlotRange -> All, 
   PlotLabel -> "Velocity"]} // Row, {{m, 1, "mass of the block"}, 1, 10, 
  1}, {{k, 100, "spring constant"}, 100, 1000, 
  100}, {{vb, 1, "belt velocity"}, 1, 10, 
  1}, {{a, 5, "friction coefficient"}, 5, 45, 10}]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
## Hybrid Differential Equations
Model a damped oscillator that gets a kick at regular time intervals:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Hybrid Differential Equations
Model a damped oscillator that gets a kick at regular time intervals:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
system = {x''[t] + .1 x'[t] + x[t] == 0, x[0] == 1, x'[0] == 0};
control = WhenEvent[Mod[t, 1] == 0, x'[t] -> x'[t] + 1];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
sol = DSolve[{system, control}, x, {t, 0, 50}];
Plot[Evaluate[{x[t], x'[t]} /. sol], {t, 0, 50}, PlotLegends->LineLegend[Automatic, {"Posiiton", "Velocity"}]]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(Legended[ToExpression[FrontEndRef["545f6ca9-eab4-45e6-8832-cedc643764b2"], InputForm], Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[Opacity[1.], RGBColor[0.24, 0.6, 0.8], AbsoluteThickness[2]], Directive[Opacity[1.], RGBColor[0.95, 0.627, 0.1425], AbsoluteThickness[2]]}, {"Posiiton", "Velocity"}, LegendMarkers -> None, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> "Column"], After, Identity]])(*,*)(*"1:"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
In a square box, model a ball that changes direction upon impact with the side walls:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
In a square box, model a ball that changes direction upon impact with the side walls:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
ClearAll[a, b, x]

sol = DSolve[
    {
        (x')[t] == a[t]
        ,
        (y')[t] == b[t]
        ,
        x[0] == 0
        ,
        y[0] == 0
        ,
        a[0] == 1
        ,
        b[0] == (*FB[*)((17)(*,*)/(*,*)(12))(*]FB*)
        ,
        WhenEvent[(*SpB[*)Power[x[t](*|*),(*|*)2](*]SpB*) == 1, a[t] -> -a[t]]
        ,
        WhenEvent[(*SpB[*)Power[y[t](*|*),(*|*)2](*]SpB*) == 1, b[t] -> -b[t]]
    }
    ,
    {x, y}
    ,
    {t, 0, 50}
    ,
    DiscreteVariables -> {a, b}
];

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
ParametricPlot[{x[t], y[t]} /. sol, {t, 0, 50}, Frame -> True, 
 FrameTicks -> None, Axes -> False]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(FrontEndRef["Fb9c356c3-21fa-47d8-ab5a-9bd1ce8b9aa6"])(*,*)(*"1:eJxTTMoPSmNkYGAoZgESHvk5KRCeEJBwK8rPK3HNS3GtSE0uLUlMykkNVgUJJ1kmG5uaJRvrGhmmJeqamKdY6CYmmSbqWialGCanWiRZJiaaAQCiyxap"*)(*]VB*)

